# Doctor (shadow)

A deliberately minimal, cheap work-alike for the built-in `/doctor` — not comprehensive, not
a replacement. It exists so rules and hooks can be iterated on
across many sessions without paying the full built-in `/doctor`'s time/token cost on every
run.

## Checks

Run the script and report its output verbatim (it's already terse — don't expand on it):

```bash
~/.claude/skills/doctor/scripts/run-checks.sh
```

1. **settings.json validity** — is `~/.claude/settings.json` present and valid JSON.
2. **Hook health** — for every `command`-type hook in `~/.claude/settings.json`, does the
   referenced script exist and is it executable.

Nothing else. No skill/plugin/MCP usage audit, no version check, no CLAUDE.md analysis, no
PATH/install check — those require either transcript mining or broader scans this skill is
explicitly not meant to pay for. Point the user at the real `/doctor` for those.
